\title{Statistical Depth Functions for Multivariate Analysis}
\description{
DepthProc implements statistical depth functions and the exploratory,
inferential and robust-estimation tools built on top of them. The entry
points below are grouped by what you have and what you want to do with it.
}
\details{
\strong{Depth of multivariate data.} \code{\link{depth}} is the central
entry point: it takes the points to score, the reference sample, and a
\code{method} naming the depth function. \code{\link{depthMedian}} returns
the deepest point, and \code{\link{depthLocal}} the local variant.

\strong{Depth of functional data.} \code{\link{fncDepth}} dispatches on the
class of its input and covers Fraiman-Muniz (\code{"FM"}) and modified band
depth (\code{"MBD"}); \code{\link{fncDepthMedian}} and
\code{\link{fncGetBand}} work on the result.

\strong{Plots.} \code{\link{ddPlot}} (depth-versus-depth),
\code{\link{depthContour}} and \code{\link{depthPersp}} for the depth
surface, \code{\link{scaleCurve}} and \code{\link{asymmetryCurve}} for
scale and asymmetry, and \code{\link{fncBoxPlot}} for functional boxplots.

\strong{Inference and estimation.} \code{\link{mWilcoxonTest}} is the
multivariate two-sample test; \code{\link{CovLP}} is a depth-weighted
scatter estimator; \code{\link{deepReg2d}} and
\code{\link{trimProjReg2d}} are robust regressions.

\strong{Other tools.} \code{\link{binningDepth2D}} for robust 2d binning,
\code{\link{depthDensity}} for depth-based density estimation,
\code{\link{lsdSampleMaxDepth}} for location-scale depth, and
\code{\link{runifsphere}} for sampling directions on a sphere.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{depth}}, \code{\link{fncDepth}}
